00:09:46,163 --> 00:09:47,605
the speed shift or something.

253
00:09:47,605 --> 00:09:48,438
- [Crow] Aw, shut up, pee wee.

254
00:09:48,438 --> 00:09:49,605
- [Joel] Yeah.

255
00:09:53,805 --> 00:09:55,682
- What kept you so long, Lisa?

256
00:09:55,682 --> 00:09:59,327
- Mr. Willis smoked two cigars
at the table after dinner.

257
00:09:59,327 --> 00:10:00,753
And I couldn't get up.

258
00:10:00,753 --> 00:10:04,138
- [Tom] Whoa, whoa, whoa,
honey, speak English, will ya?

259
00:10:04,138 --> 00:10:06,071
- Pat did not come home for this.

260
00:10:06,071 --> 00:10:08,671
That's why his father was upset.

261
00:10:08,671 --> 00:10:10,928
- [Crow] Here, drink this,
it'll make you feel American.

262
00:10:10,928 --> 00:10:12,773
- There's old man Harris.

263
00:10:12,773 --> 00:10:16,940
(Tom, Joel, & Crow humming
"The Munsters Theme")

264
00:10:19,101 --> 00:10:20,549
- That fella has a jewel of a car.

265
00:10:20,549 --> 00:10:21,816
- [Tom] Let me think about that.

266
00:10:21,816 --> 00:10:23,407
Okay.

267
00:10:23,407 --> 00:10:25,970
(laughing)

268
00:10:25,970 --> 00:10:29,714
- [Crow] Hoiman, wait here in the car!

269
00:10:29,714 --> 00:10:32,809
- [Tom] Looks like this is
where old jalopies go to die.

270
00:10:32,809 --> 00:10:35,225
- [Joel] It's TV's lovable Stringbean!

271
00:10:35,225 --> 00:10:37,398
(cheering)

272
00:10:37,398 --> 00:10:38,472
- You wanna sell that deuce?

273
00:10:38,472 --> 00:10:39,706
- [Crow] My little deuce coupe?

274
00:10:39,706 --> 00:10:41,498
You don't know what I got!

275
00:10:41,498 --> 00:10:44,833
- Why you fellers always
askin' me to buy my car?

276
00:10:44,833 --> 00:10:47,325
- That 32 is the ideal
stock to convert to a bomb.

277
00:10:47,325 --> 00:10:48,946
- [Joel] Why do you guys
always throw me down

278
00:10:48,946 --> 00:10:50,616
and steal my wallet?

279
00:10:50,616 --> 00:10:51,560
- It's just like gettin' married.

280
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:53,837
Or going to New York City.

281
00:10:53,837 --> 00:10:56,177
- [Joel, Tom, Crow] New York City!

282
00:10:56,177 --> 00:10:58,049
- [Joel] Get the rope.

283
00:10:58,049 --> 00:10:58,882
(laughing)

284
00:10:58,882 --> 00:11:00,675
Available for parties and barmitzvers.

285
00:11:00,675 --> 00:11:04,004
- I could get you a good price on that.

286
00:11:04,004 --> 00:11:05,113
- [Voiceover] Again with the finger.

287
00:11:05,113 --> 00:11:08,897
- It's $695 for that car 26 years ago.

288
00:11:08,897 --> 00:11:11,592
10 years ago, wasn't worth a dime.

289
00:11:11,592 --> 00:11:14,575
Last month, I turned down 100 for it.

290
00:11:14,575 --> 00:11:18,231
When it gets back up to
695 again, I'll sell it.

291
00:11:18,231 --> 00:11:20,481
(laughing)

292
00:11:21,669 --> 00:11:23,161
Hey Spook,

293
00:11:23,161 --> 00:11:26,218
give me a snort of that there sody pop.

294
00:11:26,218 --> 00:11:27,375
(laughing)

295
00:11:27,375 --> 00:11:28,670
- [Crow] 'Scuse me, that
one just slipped out.

296
00:11:28,670 --> 00:11:30,066
- Hey gang, you know this will be Lisa's

297
00:11:30,066 --> 00:11:31,777
first trip to a drive-in?

298
00:11:31,777 --> 00:11:33,638
- Aw, we have drive-ins in France, too.

299
00:11:33,638 --> 00:11:35,740
- [Voiceover] Wee, they
play Jerry Lewis movies.

300
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:37,628
- I went with my brother
on his motor scooter.

301
00:11:37,628 --> 00:11:39,476
(laughing)

302
00:11:39,476 --> 00:11:40,879
- [Joel] Looks like
he's filling the bottle.

303
00:11:40,879 --> 00:11:42,070
(groaning)

304
00:11:42,070 --> 00:11:45,487
- [Crow] Who put sody pop in my sody pop?

305
00:11:48,156 --> 00:11:52,360
- [Tom] Hey, let's go do some crimes, man.

306
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:54,601
- If the road's clear, I'll
drag you to Bartinell's corner.

307
00:11:54,601 --> 00:11:57,633
- [Crow] Drag me, I'll get the tow chain.

308
00:11:57,633 --> 00:11:59,084
- [Voiceover] You still
runnin' on that old rubber?

309
00:11:59,084 --> 00:12:01,183
- [Joel] Old rubber, no, no, no!

310
00:12:01,183 --> 00:12:02,912
- Hey Spook, when Pat and Liz get here,

311
00:12:02,912 --> 00:12:04,609
will you tell them we went to the drive-in

312
00:12:04,609 --> 00:12:06,525
and for them to catch up?

313
00:12:06,525 --> 00:12:07,614
Thank you.

314
00:12:07,614 --> 00:12:09,614
- We sure will.

315
00:12:09,614 --> 00:12:11,532
- And I'll give you 150 bucks.

316
00:12:11,532 --> 00:12:12,398
- [Crow] To take acting lessons.

317
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:15,484
- You're talking like my butchers.

318
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:17,192
- [Joel] Okay, 'nuff said, old timer.

319
00:12:17,192 --> 00:12:19,145
- What are you playin' with, kids?

320
00:12:19,145 --> 00:12:22,069
(laughing)

321
00:12:22,069 --> 00:12:23,496
- [Tom] Oh, it's red man juice.

322
00:12:23,496 --> 00:12:24,456
(groaning)

323
00:12:24,456 --> 00:12:25,297
- [Joel] That guy cracks me up.

324
00:12:25,297 --> 00:12:27,650
I don't know, do you?

325
00:12:27,650 --> 00:12:28,773
- [Tom] One-Adam 12, one-Adam 12,

326
00:12:28,773 --> 00:12:31,440
what are you doing in Wisconsin?

327
00:12:32,490 --> 00:12:36,465
- [Crow] Selznick International
Pictures presents.

328
00:12:36,465 --> 00:12:40,632
- [Tom] I'm Sebastian Cabot,
and this is Ghost Story.

329
00:12:47,043 --> 00:12:49,569
- [Tom] Well gel there program.

330
00:12:49,569 --> 00:12:51,386
- Pat didn't come home last night.

331
00:12:51,386 --> 00:12:52,393
- He didn't?

332
00:12:52,393 --> 00:12:54,509
- No, evidently he was
out with Liz Humphries.

333
00:12:54,509 --> 00:12:56,221
She didn't come home either.

334
00:12:56,221 --> 00:12:57,797
- [Joel] When you due, Sheriff?

335
00:12:57,797 --> 00:12:59,809
- I want you to find out why.

336
00:12:59,809 --> 00:13:02,248
And don't leave a stone
unturned in doing so.

337
00:13:02,248 --> 00:13:03,992
Do I make myself clear?

338
00:13:03,992 --> 00:13:05,758
- I understand Mr. Wheeler.

339
00:13:05,758 --> 00:13:07,336
- [Crow] That's a well fitting suit.

340
00:13:07,336 --> 00:13:09,753
- Wrecks reported last night.

341
00:13:10,795 --> 00:13:12,991
Your son, Pat, about 19 isn't he?

342
00:13:12,991 --> 00:13:14,010
- That's right.

343
00:13:14,010 --> 00:13:14,992
- [Joel] As teens go, yes.

344
00:13:14,992 --> 00:13:16,865
- A year older than I
was when I got married.

345
00:13:16,865 --> 00:13:18,015
- You think they eloped?

346
00:13:18,015 --> 00:13:20,465
- [Tom] No, they can't
elope, they're fruit, get it?

347
00:13:20,465 --> 00:13:22,132
- I didn't say that.

348
00:13:23,006 --> 00:13:24,645
But if they were out together all night,

349
00:13:24,645 --> 00:13:26,159
you better hope they have.

350
00:13:26,159 --> 00:13:27,583
- This is a missing person's report

351
00:13:27,583 --> 00:13:29,808
and I want to know what
you're going to do about it.

352
00:13:29,808 --> 00:13:33,499
- Well, I'll send in an APB
on both of them and the car.

353
00:13:33,499 --> 00:13:34,721
I don't think it'll do much good

354
00:13:34,721 --> 00:13:35,752
if they went off to get married,

355
00:13:35,752 --> 00:13:37,937
they'd already be across the state line.

356
00:13:37,937 --> 00:13:39,855
- Why, if he got married,
I'll ring his neck.

357
00:13:39,855 --> 00:13:41,257
- [Crow] That Jerry
Lee, he's done it again!

358
00:13:41,257 --> 00:13:43,583
- If you ask me, it's that Chase Winston.

359
00:13:43,583 --> 00:13:44,794
He's older than the others.

360
00:13:44,794 --> 00:13:46,561
Sets them all wrong.

361
00:13:46,561 --> 00:13:49,120
Why he's got more influence
on Pat than I have.

362
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,106
- [Tom] Hooker's a good cop.

363
00:13:50,106 --> 00:13:52,291
- Chase Winston does more
about keeping them in line

364
00:13:52,291 --> 00:13:54,463
then getting them in trouble and I know.

365
00:13:54,463 --> 00:13:55,895
He's supported his mother and sister

366
00:13:55,895 --> 00:13:59,041
ever since his dad on
one of your drill rings.

367
00:13:59,041 --> 00:14:01,703
Your son could take a page
outta his book Mr. Wheeler.

368
00:14:01,703 --> 00:14:02,536
- [Joel] Ooh, what a burn.

369
00:14:02,536 --> 00:14:05,241
- When I get through with my
son, he won't have a book left.

370
00:14:05,241 --> 00:14:07,586
Now you locate him, or I'll have your job.

371
00:14:07,586 --> 00:14:09,055
- If you want to be the only peace officer

372
00:14:09,055 --> 00:14:11,912
in 10,000 square miles
and 1,000 miles of road,

373
00:14:11,912 --> 00:14:13,234
you're welcome to it.

374
00:14:13,234 --> 00:14:15,823
- [Crow] This is my
world and welcome to it.

375
00:14:15,823 --> 00:14:18,339
- I'll do everything I can
to locate both of them.

376
00:14:18,339 --> 00:14:22,050
- [Voiceover] Go on home,
they're waiting for you.

377
00:14:22,050 --> 00:14:22,961
(barking)

378
00:14:22,961 --> 00:14:27,044
("Mystery Science Theater 3000")

379
00:14:29,909 --> 00:14:30,742
- [Voiceover] Hi Sheriff.

380
00:14:30,742 --> 00:14:31,575
- [Crow] Wish I were.

381
00:14:31,575 --> 00:14:33,825
(laughing)

382
00:14:37,058 --> 00:14:39,531
- [Tom] What is this, The
Misfits all of the sudden?

383
00:14:39,531 --> 00:14:41,031
- Yeah, new to me.

384
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:43,097
That's the biker I am.

385
00:14:43,097 --> 00:14:46,314
I'd be chasin' bicycles a couple of days.

386
00:14:46,314 --> 00:14:47,719
- Aw, come on Sheriff.

387
00:14:47,719 --> 00:14:48,587
Outside of Pat Wheeler,

388
00:14:48,587 --> 00:14:51,355
we haven't had a ticket in
our gang in eight months.

389
00:14:51,355 --> 00:14:53,083
- I was just kidding.

390
00:14:53,083 --> 00:14:55,277
- [Joel] How much for
the macaroni and cheese.

391
00:14:55,277 --> 00:14:56,742
- What's the mileage on it?

392
00:14:56,742 --> 00:14:59,102
- Oh, about 35,000.

393
00:14:59,102 --> 00:15:00,812
Tell him you bought it from the state.

394
00:15:00,812 --> 00:15:04,649
Those lucky stiffs on highway
get a new car every year.

395
00:15:04,649 --> 00:15:05,913
- Let me have it for a couple of days

396
00:15:05,913 --> 00:15:07,187
and I'll tune it up for you.

397
00:15:07,187 --> 00:15:08,552
(laughing)

398
00:15:08,552 --> 00:15:10,990
- You'd joke it off so
I could never catch it.

399
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:14,467
- You couldn't catch that
deuce of mine right now.

400
00:15:14,467 --> 00:15:16,210
Now let me have that patrol car.

401
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:18,679
I'll turn it into a slingshot
that'll catch anything.

402
00:15:18,679 --> 00:15:21,846
- [Tom] A Joe Namath netted slingshot.

403
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:26,089
(grunting)

404
00:15:28,019 --> 00:15:30,438
- [Joel] What do you dream about?

405
00:15:30,438 --> 00:15:32,606
- Just between us, Liz
Humphries and Pat Wheeler

406
00:15:32,606 --> 00:15:35,689
didn't get home last night.

407
00:15:35,689 --> 00:15:37,061
- They were supposed to
meet us at the drive-in

408
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:38,631
but they didn't show up.

409
00:15:38,631 --> 00:15:40,322
I wondered what happened.

410
00:15:40,322 --> 00:15:41,424
- [Tom] Hec Ramsey!

411
00:15:41,424 --> 00:15:44,350
- Are they in any kind of trouble?

412
00:15:44,350 --> 00:15:46,286
- What do you mean?

413
00:15:46,286 --> 00:15:47,203
- You know.

414
00:15:48,602 --> 00:15:52,052
- [Joel] You know, like Warren
Beatty and Annette Bening?

415
00:15:52,052 --> 00:15:53,969
- No, I don't think so.

416
00:15:54,975 --> 00:15:57,480
- Chase, level with me.

417
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:58,339
- [Crow] You think I'm pretty?

418
00:15:58,339 --> 00:16:00,493
- I'm almost positive they
weren't in any trouble.

419
00:16:00,493 --> 00:16:01,564
I'd know.

420
00:16:01,564 --> 00:16:02,868
- [Joel] Mechanics intuition.

421
00:16:02,868 --> 00:16:06,464
- You think they might've
run off to get married?

422
00:16:06,464 --> 00:16:09,312
- They've been going
steady for over a year now.

423
00:16:09,312 --> 00:16:11,404
I know they talked about it.

424
00:16:11,404 --> 00:16:13,060
- [Tom] Well sir, person's got urges.

425
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:14,934
- Not for right now.

426
00:16:14,934 --> 00:16:16,553
- Did Pat have any money saved?

427
00:16:16,553 --> 00:16:18,839
- [Crow] Jeez, what is
he, the Shell Answer Man?

428
00:16:18,839 --> 00:16:20,155
- Yeah, some.

429
00:16:20,155 --> 00:16:21,921
- Like how much?

430
00:16:21,921 --> 00:16:23,732
- Well, he was talkin'
about gettin' a new blower,

431
00:16:23,732 --> 00:16:24,649
and a mill.

432
00:16:25,517 --> 00:16:27,200
About 500 bucks.

433
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,821
- Where did he get that kind of money?

434
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:31,071
- [Crow] Bake sale.
- Saved it.

435
00:16:31,071 --> 00:16:32,517
His old man gives him a good allowance

436
00:16:32,517 --> 00:16:34,753
when he's not mad at him.

437
00:16:34,753 --> 00:16:36,295
- What bank does he use?

438
00:16:36,295 --> 00:16:40,564
- [Tom] Hooterville Savings and Loan, why?

439
00:16:40,564 --> 00:16:43,526
- Could've saved it to
get married, could he?

440
00:16:43,526 --> 00:16:45,976
- I guess he can do
whatever he wants with it.

441
00:16:45,976 --> 00:16:49,926
- [Joel] Looks like the
garage of Doctor Caligari.

442
00:16:49,926 --> 00:16:51,864
- His old man put him down flat.

443
00:16:51,864 --> 00:16:53,240
- I know.

444
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,281
But Pat's smart enough
to provide for himself

445
00:16:55,281 --> 00:16:57,614
'til his old man cooled off.

446
00:16:58,506 --> 00:17:01,096
- [Joel] Dong, dong, dong.
- [Crow] Sanctuary! Sanctuary!

447
00:17:01,096 --> 00:17:03,595
- Did you check the hospitals?

448
00:17:03,595 --> 00:17:04,428
- Yeah.

449
00:17:05,418 --> 00:17:07,548
Where could I find the rest of the gang?

450
00:17:07,548 --> 00:17:08,648
- [Joel] Gang land?

451
00:17:08,648 --> 00:17:09,907
- I don't know about Bob and Gordi,

452
00:17:09,907 --> 00:17:11,860
but Chuck and Rec went over to Easton.

453
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:13,531
They wanted to check with the Wheel Cats

454
00:17:13,531 --> 00:17:15,217
about next Saturday night's platter party.

455
00:17:15,217 --> 00:17:16,335
- Next Saturday night?

456
00:17:16,335 --> 00:17:17,611
- Yeah.

457
00:17:17,611 --> 00:17:19,286
- You warn the gang I'll be cruising

458
00:17:19,286 --> 00:17:20,759
that pass that night.

459
00:17:20,759 --> 00:17:22,379
No draggin'.

460
00:17:22,379 --> 00:17:24,785
- [Joel] Aw, and he just
bought those red, satin pumps.

461
00:17:24,785 --> 00:17:28,074
- You get any postcards
from those two, let me know.

462
00:17:28,074 --> 00:17:31,324
- [Crow] Say, nice J. Crew barn jacket.

463
00:17:32,754 --> 00:17:34,485
- [Tom] Meanwhile, at
Grandma's lake cottage

464
00:17:34,485 --> 00:17:36,402
in Frederic, Wisconsin.

465
00:17:41,410 --> 00:17:42,351
- Hi Sheriff!

466
00:17:42,351 --> 00:17:43,389
- [Joel] Hey Mr. Douglas,

467
00:17:43,389 --> 00:17:46,625
I got those bodies buried just in time.

468
00:17:46,625 --> 00:17:48,989
(door knocking)

469
00:17:48,989 --> 00:17:50,184
- [Tom] Were just waiting by the door?

470
00:17:50,184 --> 00:17:51,017
- [Joel] Junior Samples!

471
00:17:51,017 --> 00:17:53,022
- Hello Sheriff.

472
00:17:53,022 --> 00:17:54,720
(Crow yelling)

473
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:55,723
- She's a good girl, Sheriff.

474
00:17:55,723 --> 00:17:56,556
- [Crow] God, you're ugly.

475
00:17:56,556 --> 00:17:58,756
- How come you drove around
the truck all night, then?

476
00:17:58,756 --> 00:18:01,592
- [Joel] Well, let's just say
I'm acquainted with the night.

477
00:18:01,592 --> 00:18:03,400
- You don't think she might've eloped?

478
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,233
- Could be.

479
00:18:04,233 --> 00:18:06,240
She's pretty closed-mouth
about her affairs.

480
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:07,579
- Maude likes a Wheeler.

481
00:18:07,579 --> 00:18:09,006
He ain't marrying our kind.

482
00:18:09,006 --> 00:18:10,966
- [Tom] Here's we're just
simple white trash folk.

483
00:18:10,966 --> 00:18:12,358
- Just dropped around to let you know

484
00:18:12,358 --> 00:18:13,880
I'm doing everything I can.

485
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:14,829
- We know that Sheriff.

486
00:18:14,829 --> 00:18:16,515
We sure do appreciate it.

487
00:18:16,515 --> 00:18:19,273
(spitting)

488
00:18:19,273 --> 00:18:21,465
- Never had any trouble
lookin' after kids.

489
00:18:21,465 --> 00:18:23,286
- Let me know if I can help, Sheriff.

490
00:18:23,286 --> 00:18:25,453
(blaring)

491
00:18:26,378 --> 00:18:27,227
- [Man] Quit worryin' this way.

492
00:18:27,227 --> 00:18:28,249
Got to trust in the Lord.

493
00:18:28,249 --> 00:18:30,416
- [Crow] Crazy Amish folk.

494
00:18:32,905 --> 00:18:37,278
(Tom, Joel, & Crow humming
"The Munsters Theme")

495
00:18:37,278 --> 00:18:39,238
- Morning Sheriff.

496
00:18:39,238 --> 00:18:41,829
- Let me smell your breath.

497
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:42,891
- [Crow] Nice uvula.

498
00:18:42,891 --> 00:18:44,308
- Okay, go ahead.

499
00:18:45,859 --> 00:18:49,192
- [Joel] Set me free, booze, I need you.

500
00:18:56,245 --> 00:18:57,609
- Hi Chase.
- [Chase] Hi.

501
00:18:57,609 --> 00:18:58,793
- [Crow] Still got your knee up, I see.

502
00:18:58,793 --> 00:18:59,979
- Yeah, she's all set.

503
00:18:59,979 --> 00:19:00,812
- Good.

504
00:19:01,934 --> 00:19:03,426
My boy, that's one trip

505
00:19:03,426 --> 00:19:05,386
I'm glad I don't have to make very often.

506
00:19:05,386 --> 00:19:06,219
- The stuff heavy?

507
00:19:06,219 --> 00:19:07,215
I'll help you unload.

508
00:19:07,215 --> 00:19:08,965
- [Tom] Ready and up!

509
00:19:09,802 --> 00:19:11,792
- Wheeler's takin' that oil well

510
00:19:11,792 --> 00:19:14,184
and he's afraid of fire when he comes in.

511
00:19:14,184 --> 00:19:17,351
- [Crow] What the heck are you saying?

512
00:19:18,885 --> 00:19:21,183
- Wants us to keep it
out back in store hours.

513
00:19:21,183 --> 00:19:24,830
- [Tom] Will Rogers Follies
will continue after this.

514
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:27,744
- I made $100 for that stuff.

515
00:19:27,744 --> 00:19:29,138
Dad showed me how to use it.

516
00:19:29,138 --> 00:19:32,648
- [Tom] Mom told you not to use it.

517
00:19:32,648 --> 00:19:35,504
- Well, I'm sorry I was late gettin' back.

518
00:19:35,504 --> 00:19:37,263
With that cargo, I was afraid to do

519
00:19:37,263 --> 00:19:38,519
five miles an hour.

520
00:19:38,519 --> 00:19:41,220
- [Crow] Was English your first language?

521
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:44,346
- It's not dangerous as long
as it's in a nitro case.

522
00:19:44,346 --> 00:19:45,836
- But I took these outta the case.

523
00:19:45,836 --> 00:19:47,480
(gasping)

524
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:50,029
- You're lucky to be
standing talkin' about it.

525
00:19:50,029 --> 00:19:51,418
- [Voiceover] Hey, don't go away sore,

526
00:19:51,418 --> 00:19:53,251
let's talk it through.

527
00:19:56,828 --> 00:19:57,661
- [Tom] Oh, hi mom.

528
00:19:57,661 --> 00:19:59,608
Hey, don't get up, here's
your chili and your water.

529
00:19:59,608 --> 00:20:01,224
- [Crow] Did we win the war son?

530
00:20:01,224 --> 00:20:02,495
- [Tom] Shut up, mom.

531
00:20:02,495 --> 00:20:03,662
- [Crow] Okay.

532
00:20:05,116 --> 00:20:06,340
- My tax in the safe now?

533
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:08,259
- [Crow] Get your knee up, boy, c'mon.

534
00:20:08,259 --> 00:20:09,259
There we go.

535
00:20:11,598 --> 00:20:14,384
- Is that nitro safe out there?

536
00:20:14,384 --> 00:20:16,710
- If it decides to blow,
it's not safe anywhere.

537
00:20:16,710 --> 00:20:18,059
- [Crow] Is it safe?

538
00:20:18,059 --> 00:20:20,240
(ringing)

539
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,982
- [Tom] My knee's ringing.

540
00:20:21,982 --> 00:20:22,981
- I'll get it.

541
00:20:22,981 --> 00:20:24,528
- That's not our ring.

542
00:20:24,528 --> 00:20:26,276
- No, it's the Sheriff's.

543
00:20:26,276 --> 00:20:28,499
If there's been a wreck,
I get a tow job out of it.

544
00:20:28,499 --> 00:20:29,749
- [Tom] Oh wow.

545
00:20:31,233 --> 00:20:34,072
- You work all the
angles, don't you, Chase?

546
00:20:34,072 --> 00:20:35,614
- Mr. Compton, I have to.

547
00:20:35,614 --> 00:20:38,364
- [Crow] He's a geometry teacher.

548
00:20:40,496 --> 00:20:43,329
Oh yes (panting).

549
00:20:46,441 --> 00:20:47,472
What are you wearing?

550
00:20:47,472 --> 00:20:50,222
I'm putting my knee up right now.

551
00:20:54,692 --> 00:20:56,525
- [Tom] Sweet erosion.

552
00:20:59,801 --> 00:21:01,013
(heavy breathing)

553
00:21:01,013 --> 00:21:03,352
We've heard enough!

554
00:21:03,352 --> 00:21:05,435
- [Crow] I feel so dirty.

555
00:21:06,328 --> 00:21:08,084
- There's been a wreck,
12 miles out of town.

556
00:21:08,084 --> 00:21:09,109
Where's the wrecker?

557
00:21:09,109 --> 00:21:13,004
- Oh, I used the A frame to
build a doggone rock garden.

558
00:21:13,004 --> 00:21:15,485
Look, you take your car and
keep the city's records off.

559
00:21:15,485 --> 00:21:16,984
I'll get our wreck and follow you.

560
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:18,126
- [Tom] And we can clear away

561
00:21:18,126 --> 00:21:20,683
the wreckage of our sordid past.

562
00:21:20,683 --> 00:21:22,470
(police siren blaring)

563
00:21:22,470 --> 00:21:24,137
- [Tom] N. Y. P. D.!

564
00:21:27,546 --> 00:21:28,702
We know you're here.

565
00:21:28,702 --> 00:21:31,176
There's no one else in the
county and you use your siren.

566
00:21:31,176 --> 00:21:33,275
(laughing)

567
00:21:33,275 --> 00:21:37,442
- [Crow] They've got this
angled parking thing all wrong.

568
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:42,584
- [Tom] Is there anything I can
put my knee up on here, boy?

569
00:21:42,584 --> 00:21:45,041
- I wondered who was on
that party line a while ago.

570
00:21:45,041 --> 00:21:47,260
- Cost me to get on that line with you.

571
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:49,283
I figured since it was on
your call station anyway,

572
00:21:49,283 --> 00:21:50,819
you wouldn't care.

573
00:21:50,819 --> 00:21:52,286
- There's a pretty good one.

574
00:21:52,286 --> 00:21:53,854
- Yeah.

575
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:56,229
- [Tom] Looks like a cat
climbed up on the grill, woof.

576
00:21:56,229 --> 00:21:58,646
- [Sheriff] This engine's still warm.

577
00:21:58,646 --> 00:22:00,672
- Say, did you see the
skid marks out here?

578
00:22:00,672 --> 00:22:02,014
They go at a direct right angle

579
00:22:02,014 --> 00:22:04,101
than the direction of travel.

580
00:22:04,101 --> 00:22:07,470
- [Crow] Hey, sounds like
Robert Klein's around here.

581
00:22:07,470 --> 00:22:09,069
- No digs in the mechanum either.

582
00:22:09,069 --> 00:22:10,736
- [Tom] Sad, really.

583
00:22:13,869 --> 00:22:15,014
- [Sheriff] Somebody was hurt in here,

584
00:22:15,014 --> 00:22:16,802
there's blood all over the upholstery.

585
00:22:16,802 --> 00:22:18,867
- [Tom] Nothing scapes
you, oldie, does it?

586
00:22:18,867 --> 00:22:20,721
- There's nobody here.

587
00:22:20,721 --> 00:22:21,825
- Real good?

588
00:22:21,825 --> 00:22:23,325
- Yeah, real good.

589
00:22:24,531 --> 00:22:26,337
Well, maybe somebody came
by and picked them up.

590
00:22:26,337 --> 00:22:28,607
Could've been the people that called in.

591
00:22:28,607 --> 00:22:31,698
- No, they'd of said something.

592
00:22:31,698 --> 00:22:33,409
- Then why didn't they wait?

593
00:22:33,409 --> 00:22:35,346
- People who go to the
trouble to report an accident

594
00:22:35,346 --> 00:22:36,282
but they won't stay around,

595
00:22:36,282 --> 00:22:38,174
don't want to fill out the reports.

596
00:22:38,174 --> 00:22:39,782
- [Tom] Yeah, nobody likes a lousy snitch.

597
00:22:39,782 --> 00:22:43,527
- Well, I'll take the license
number and engine number.

598
00:22:43,527 --> 00:22:44,770
Call headquarters.

599
00:22:44,770 --> 00:22:45,603
Maybe they've got

600
00:22:45,603 --> 00:22:49,186
a line on 'em.
- [Tom] You are headquarters.

601
00:22:50,416 --> 00:22:51,970
- [Crow] Hey, what are you looking at?

602
00:22:51,970 --> 00:22:53,759
That's official police property.

603
00:22:53,759 --> 00:22:54,778
- How are you headlights.

604
00:22:54,778 --> 00:22:56,876
- [Joel] I don't have head lice.

605
00:22:56,876 --> 00:22:58,709
- Both of 'em burning?

606
00:23:02,607 --> 00:23:04,550
How many times have I warned you

607
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,443
about gettin' that headlamp fixed?

608
00:23:06,443 --> 00:23:07,717
- [Joel] About a ka-jillion, sir.

609
00:23:07,717 --> 00:23:10,375
- But the first time it
was just a suggestion.

610
00:23:10,375 --> 00:23:13,135
- COB only costs four dollars.

611
00:23:13,135 --> 00:23:15,034
- [Voiceover] The tender headlight theme.

612
00:23:15,034 --> 00:23:16,975
(whimpering)

613
00:23:16,975 --> 00:23:18,412
- Missy?

614
00:23:18,412 --> 00:23:19,559
- The doctor said she'd be able

615
00:23:19,559 --> 00:23:20,892
to start walking again pretty soon,

616
00:23:20,892 --> 00:23:25,059
took all I had to make a part
down payment on her braces.

617
00:23:26,171 --> 00:23:27,203
- [Joel] Gosh, the moonlight

618
00:23:27,203 --> 00:23:29,971
does crazy things to your hair, sir.

619
00:23:29,971 --> 00:23:32,224
- Well, I think this
is a complete wash out.

620
00:23:32,224 --> 00:23:33,654
- [Tom] These folks are dead,
not much else we can do.

621
00:23:33,654 --> 00:23:34,875
- You probably got a screwdriver.

622
00:23:34,875 --> 00:23:36,405
- [Joel] No, but I've
got a Singapore Sling.

623
00:23:36,405 --> 00:23:37,238
- [Tom] Ba-boons.

624
00:23:37,238 --> 00:23:38,870
- I don't think the insurance company

625
00:23:38,870 --> 00:23:40,507
would miss one of those headlamps.

626
00:23:40,507 --> 00:23:41,920
- [Tom] Yeah, that guy's not gonna miss

627
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,753
his credit cards either, you know?

628
00:23:55,814 --> 00:23:57,423
- [Crow & Tom] Hey, one, two, one, two.

629
00:23:57,423 --> 00:23:59,348
- Come on, Crow, Lindy.

630
00:23:59,348 --> 00:24:00,918
Ow, your beak.

631
00:24:00,918 --> 00:24:01,953
- What about my beak?

632
00:24:01,953 --> 00:24:02,786
- Big ol' beak.

633
00:24:02,786 --> 00:24:04,323
- Hey, hey, you guys quiet down.

634
00:24:04,323 --> 00:24:06,307
Hi, do you like to make money?

635
00:24:06,307 --> 00:24:07,683
Sure, we all do.

636
00:24:07,683 --> 00:24:09,010
Well, do you realize,

637
00:24:09,010 --> 00:24:09,843
hey, move aside,

638
00:24:09,843 --> 00:24:12,111
do you realize you might have a goldmine

639
00:24:12,111 --> 00:24:15,184
sitting in that empty pantry
or linen closet at home?

640
00:24:15,184 --> 00:24:16,962
Yeah, sure, just do what I do

641
00:24:16,962 --> 00:24:20,507
and turn that empty closet
space into a gold mine

642
00:24:20,507 --> 00:24:23,585
by turning it into a teen
pavilion slash barber shop,

643
00:24:23,585 --> 00:24:26,219
just like in today's movie
The Giant Gila Monster.

644
00:24:26,219 --> 00:24:27,370
(cheering)

645
00:24:27,370 --> 00:24:28,665
- Silent gone, Jasper.

646
00:24:28,665 --> 00:24:29,742
- Couple of freaks down here.

647
00:24:29,742 --> 00:24:32,040
- Kids, will you step aside.

648
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:33,895
You guys and their teen lingo.

649
00:24:33,895 --> 00:24:35,908
You know, all you gotta do is clear away

650
00:24:35,908 --> 00:24:37,863
some of the more hazardous cleanser,

651
00:24:37,863 --> 00:24:40,332
stock up on plenty of
health-licious and delicious

652
00:24:40,332 --> 00:24:43,041
snacks and beverages and
then tune in your prop radio

653
00:24:43,041 --> 00:24:45,409
into the appropriate teen dance tune.

654
00:24:45,409 --> 00:24:46,997
(cheering)

655
00:24:46,997 --> 00:24:48,400
- You make me sweat, Tommy.

656
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:49,329
- Me too, ha.

657
00:24:49,329 --> 00:24:50,909
Let's go get something cool and slippery

658
00:24:50,909 --> 00:24:52,241
from the stupid jerk.

659
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:53,074
- Oh, good idea.

660
00:24:53,074 --> 00:24:53,907
- [Tom] Stupid jerk here.

661
00:24:53,907 --> 00:24:54,799
- Tom, it's soda jerk,

662
00:24:54,799 --> 00:24:57,465
would you guys straighten up
and fly with me on this one?

663
00:24:57,465 --> 00:25:00,052
Come on, this is my sketch.

664
00:25:00,052 --> 00:25:02,233
- All right, pops.

665
00:25:02,233 --> 00:25:04,411
Shoot us a couple of Blue Floyds.

666
00:25:04,411 --> 00:25:06,211
- What's a Blue Floyd?

667
00:25:06,211 --> 00:25:07,805
- Crammedy this guy.

668
00:25:07,805 --> 00:25:10,182
- Okay, daddy, we'll talk you through.

669
00:25:10,182 --> 00:25:12,213
Just put two scoops of
ice cream in a blender.

670
00:25:12,213 --> 00:25:13,658
- No, three scoops, three scoops.

671
00:25:13,658 --> 00:25:16,146
- Oh yeah, three scoops.

672
00:25:16,146 --> 00:25:17,116
Add some malted milk.
- [Joel] Three scoops

673
00:25:17,116 --> 00:25:18,950
of ice cream.

674
00:25:18,950 --> 00:25:21,483
- Then fill the top with
cool, menthol barber-cide.

675
00:25:21,483 --> 00:25:23,156
- And garnish with a comb.

676
00:25:23,156 --> 00:25:25,726
- Oh, come on you guys, that's it.

677
00:25:25,726 --> 00:25:27,228
The fun time's over.

678
00:25:27,228 --> 00:25:28,446
This is my sketch,

679
00:25:28,446 --> 00:25:30,362
you guys never go along
with me on these things.

680
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:32,200
I stop, I quit it.

681
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,469
- Come on, Joel.
- [Crow] Come on, baby.

682
00:25:33,469 --> 00:25:35,659
We're just funnin' ya.

683
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:38,364
- Every time you guys the
robots come up with some

684
00:25:38,364 --> 00:25:41,672
half-baked idea I try to go
along with it and be supportive,

685
00:25:41,672 --> 00:25:45,271
but the minute Joel has an
idea for a presentation,

686
00:25:45,271 --> 00:25:48,536
in run the baby Teddy
Ruxpins and spoil everything.

687
00:25:48,536 --> 00:25:50,996
- Okay, fine, next time
you can get your precious

688
00:25:50,996 --> 00:25:52,496
Gypsy to help you.

689
00:25:54,209 --> 00:25:56,410
- Hey Gypsy, come here.

690
00:25:56,410 --> 00:25:58,393
- [Crow] Gypsy, no, it's too small.

691
00:25:58,393 --> 00:26:00,560
(yelling)

692
00:26:01,467 --> 00:26:03,669
- These two, nothin' but trouble.

693
00:26:03,669 --> 00:26:04,941
Back after this.

694
00:26:04,941 --> 00:26:09,024
("Mystery Science Theater 3000")

695
00:26:10,128 --> 00:26:12,545
(whimpering)

696
00:26:15,490 --> 00:26:19,657
- [Joel] Just be quiet,
don't let it happen again.

697
00:26:20,839 --> 00:26:22,340
- [Tom] It's young Jimmy
Morrison as the lizard king.

698
00:26:22,340 --> 00:26:25,610
- [Crow] Here comes Fred Sanford.

699
00:26:25,610 --> 00:26:27,219
- [Tom] I'm feeling mighty peckish.

700
00:26:27,219 --> 00:26:28,136
Snack time.

701
00:26:30,395 --> 00:26:31,354
- [Joel] Good afternoon, sir or madam,

702
00:26:31,354 --> 00:26:33,283
I'd like to show you
Encyclopedia Britannica

703
00:26:33,283 --> 00:26:34,474
if you just take a--

704
00:26:34,474 --> 00:26:38,169
- [Tom] Damn, I thought
selling door to door was hard.

705
00:26:38,169 --> 00:26:39,972
- [Crow] I just love dining al fresco.

706
00:26:39,972 --> 00:26:41,636
- [Joel] And that's the
guy's name, Al Fresco,

707
00:26:41,636 --> 00:26:44,036
can you believe it?

708
00:26:44,036 --> 00:26:48,690
- [Crow] I can't get that tune
outta my head, I don't know.

709
00:26:48,690 --> 00:26:50,393
- [Tom] The road company
of Death of a Salesman

710
00:26:50,393 --> 00:26:52,143
ladies and gentlemen.

711
00:26:53,530 --> 00:26:55,625
- [Crow] I'll eat him
with relish (laughing).

712
00:26:55,625 --> 00:26:57,020
Lizard jokes.

713
00:26:57,020 --> 00:26:58,825
- [Tom] Fava beans.

714
00:26:58,825 --> 00:27:02,536
- [Joel] C. Everett Koop,
I've been meaning to quit.

715
00:27:02,536 --> 00:27:04,536
It's a Montclair Moment!

716
00:27:06,142 --> 00:27:07,478
- [Crow] Hey, can I bum a smoke?

717
00:27:07,478 --> 00:27:09,811
(screaming)

718
00:27:11,084 --> 00:27:12,177
- [Tom] And for killing that salesman,

719
00:27:12,177 --> 00:27:14,760
you win this Samsonite luggage.

720
00:27:16,199 --> 00:27:17,475
Oh, have an accident?

721
00:27:17,475 --> 00:27:20,002
No thanks, just had one.

722
00:27:20,002 --> 00:27:22,397
- Car was going out of state.

723
00:27:22,397 --> 00:27:23,984
- [Crow] Insured by Allstate.

724
00:27:23,984 --> 00:27:25,276
- [Sheriff] So whoever's
stole it is hurt or not

725
00:27:25,276 --> 00:27:26,631
as long as they can navigate.

726
00:27:26,631 --> 00:27:27,972
- [Tom] I'm a poet and I don't know it.

727
00:27:27,972 --> 00:27:29,712
- Is there anything else
I can do here, Sheriff?

728
00:27:29,712 --> 00:27:31,523
If not, I'll get this back to the garage.

729
00:27:31,523 --> 00:27:32,440
- Go ahead.

730
00:27:33,489 --> 00:27:35,171
Chase, you give me a hand?

731
00:27:35,171 --> 00:27:36,262
- [Crow] No, cinch up
your own pants, Sheriff.

732
00:27:36,262 --> 00:27:38,258
- Those skid marks.

733
00:27:38,258 --> 00:27:39,780
You stand by them for scale.

734
00:27:39,780 --> 00:27:42,736
- [Tom] Skid marks, you're
a sick man, Sheriff.

735
00:27:42,736 --> 00:27:45,153
- [Joel] Wait, that's my car!

736
00:27:50,395 --> 00:27:52,506
- [Crow] Let's see, I
got tires, headlights,

737
00:27:52,506 --> 00:27:55,089
now if I could just get a roof.

738
00:27:56,074 --> 00:27:59,741
- [Joel] Man, night
falls fast in Tennessee.

739
00:28:00,780 --> 00:28:04,947
- [Tom] I'm guessing a Northwest
flight passed overhead.

740
00:28:09,045 --> 00:28:11,721
- [Crow] Entrapment, I smell a frame up.

741
00:28:11,721 --> 00:28:12,804
Luggage cake.

742
00:28:15,609 --> 00:28:17,892
- [Tom] Can I see your
claim check, please?

743
00:28:17,892 --> 00:28:19,086
Yeah.

744
00:28:19,086 --> 00:28:20,240
- Trouble Chase?

745
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:21,265
- Don't know, Sheriff.

746
00:28:21,265 --> 00:28:22,342
Take a look.

747
00:28:22,342 --> 00:28:23,841
- [Tom] That's an easy
one, it's a suitcase.

748
00:28:23,841 --> 00:28:26,019
- Probably fell off a car.

749
00:28:26,019 --> 00:28:27,332
- No scratches on it.

750
00:28:27,332 --> 00:28:29,430
- Well, maybe it landed in a bush.

751
00:28:29,430 --> 00:28:30,263
- [Tom] You know, a smart fella

752
00:28:30,263 --> 00:28:33,430
could put his knee up on such a thing.

753
00:28:34,804 --> 00:28:36,906
- Was it just like that when you found it?

754
00:28:36,906 --> 00:28:38,713
- [Crow] When I angled it two degrees to.

755
00:28:38,713 --> 00:28:41,703
- Probably belonged to some hitchhiker.

756
00:28:41,703 --> 00:28:42,536
- [Tom] That's a leap of faith.

757
00:28:42,536 --> 00:28:43,479
- Might've belonged to that fella

758
00:28:43,479 --> 00:28:46,396
that stole that car and wrecked it.

759
00:28:48,482 --> 00:28:49,883
- [Joel] Go ahead, pick it up one of ya,

760
00:28:49,883 --> 00:28:51,174
you know you wanna.

761
00:28:51,174 --> 00:28:52,122
- [Tom] Go on!

762
00:28:52,122 --> 00:28:54,291
- Gotta say, look at this.

763
00:28:54,291 --> 00:28:58,036
- [Tom] Looks like Edward R.
Murrow's been through here.

764
00:28:58,036 --> 00:29:01,210
- [Joel] I specialize in
previously owned cigarette butts.

765
00:29:01,210 --> 00:29:03,430
- [Sheriff] Half a pack of cigarettes.

766
00:29:03,430 --> 00:29:04,263
One unlit.

767
00:29:05,186 --> 00:29:06,410
- [Tom] I can't decide which one to eat,

768
00:29:06,410 --> 00:29:08,327
they both look so good!

769
00:29:09,712 --> 00:29:12,114
- That suitcase don't
belong to any car thief,

770
00:29:12,114 --> 00:29:14,892
he was around here too long.

771
00:29:14,892 --> 00:29:16,085
I'll take it in.

772
00:29:16,085 --> 00:29:17,482
- I'll put it in the car for you.

773
00:29:17,482 --> 00:29:19,129
- Somebody will be around to claim it.

774
00:29:19,129 --> 00:29:20,036
See you later, son.

775
00:29:20,036 --> 00:29:20,869
- Right, Sheriff.

776
00:29:20,869 --> 00:29:22,633
(eerie music)

777
00:29:22,633 --> 00:29:23,466
- [Crow] Son.

778
00:29:23,466 --> 00:29:24,775
Wait, he called me son!

779
00:29:24,775 --> 00:29:26,731
No wonder Mom cries when
I mention the sheriff.

780
00:29:26,731 --> 00:29:29,231
(eerie music)

781
00:29:33,592 --> 00:29:34,900
- [Joel] You know, when
I look at the human race,

782
00:29:34,900 --> 00:29:35,733
I gotta laugh.

783
00:29:35,733 --> 00:29:36,985
I got a chickpea for a brain

784
00:29:36,985 --> 00:29:38,407
and I'm still smarter
than they are, go figure.

785
00:29:38,407 --> 00:29:41,563
I'll be right back after these words.

786
00:29:41,563 --> 00:29:44,063
(car driving)

787
00:29:46,125 --> 00:29:48,269
- [Crow] 1313 Mockingbird Lane.

788
00:29:48,269 --> 00:29:49,129
- [Tom] I'd say it looks like he's early

789
00:29:49,129 --> 00:29:51,712
for the panty raid on the dorm.

790
00:29:53,525 --> 00:29:57,692
- [Joel] Oh, thank goodness the
IHOP's still open, you know?

791
00:29:58,953 --> 00:30:00,442
- [Tom] Pancakes are up for everybody.

792
00:30:00,442 --> 00:30:02,692
(cheering)

793
00:30:04,555 --> 00:30:06,471
- [Joel] Well, it's just about
time for him to put his knee,

794
00:30:06,471 --> 00:30:07,304
(clapping and laughing)

795
00:30:07,304 --> 00:30:08,137
yup, called it!

796
00:30:08,137 --> 00:30:09,811
- [Tom] How'd you call that?

797
00:30:09,811 --> 00:30:13,978
- [Crow] Ooh-la-la, Rooty
Tooty Fresh 'n Fruity for me!

798
00:30:17,736 --> 00:30:19,964
Were you putting your knee up again?

799
00:30:19,964 --> 00:30:21,198
Aren't I enough for you?

800
00:30:21,198 --> 00:30:22,338
- Hey.

801
00:30:22,338 --> 00:30:23,648
- [Tom] Hey, you're getting
Dippity-Do on my coat.

802
00:30:23,648 --> 00:30:24,855
- I got your phone call.

803
00:30:24,855 --> 00:30:26,724
- When I was serving
dinner to Mr. Wheeler,

804
00:30:26,724 --> 00:30:28,834
he became very angry.

805
00:30:28,834 --> 00:30:30,134
He said if I saw you again

806
00:30:30,134 --> 00:30:32,088
he would have me sent back to France.

807
00:30:32,088 --> 00:30:33,220
- He can't do that.

808
00:30:33,220 --> 00:30:34,657
- Oh yes, he can.

809
00:30:34,657 --> 00:30:36,214
He's my sponsor.

810
00:30:36,214 --> 00:30:38,345
He put up the barn.

811
00:30:38,345 --> 00:30:39,345
- That was to guarantee

812
00:30:39,345 --> 00:30:41,332
that you wouldn't become
a warden of the state.

813
00:30:41,332 --> 00:30:42,165
- [Tom] Burt Ward?

814
00:30:42,165 --> 00:30:43,338
- But we don't have to
worry about any of that.

815
00:30:43,338 --> 00:30:44,561
You know how to speak English well enough

816
00:30:44,561 --> 00:30:45,827
to get a job anywhere.

817
00:30:45,827 --> 00:30:46,994
- [Crow] Yeah, maybe at a seven 11.

818
00:30:46,994 --> 00:30:47,985
- [Tom] Doh!

819
00:30:47,985 --> 00:30:49,905
- What's you worry 'bout?

820
00:30:49,905 --> 00:30:50,738
- Nothing.

821
00:30:52,601 --> 00:30:54,383
- I don't want to go with it.

822
00:30:54,383 --> 00:30:56,101
(smacking)
- You won't have to, honey.

823
00:30:56,101 --> 00:30:56,934
(burping)

824
00:30:56,934 --> 00:30:59,434
- He'll think it's your
fault Pat ran away.

825
00:30:59,434 --> 00:31:02,191
- Well, he can think
whatever he wants to think.

826
00:31:02,191 --> 00:31:05,624
- [Tom] Here, let's go
rent The Errand Boy.

827
00:31:05,624 --> 00:31:07,560
- We hadn't better take any chances.

828
00:31:07,560 --> 00:31:09,375
You go back inside,

829
00:31:09,375 --> 00:31:11,036
and look, don't worry.

830
00:31:11,036 --> 00:31:13,096
Everything's going to be okay.

831
00:31:13,096 --> 00:31:13,951
- [Joel] What the.

832
00:31:13,951 --> 00:31:16,701
French people sure do kiss funny.

833
00:31:17,629 --> 00:31:19,024
(cars driving)

834
00:31:19,024 --> 00:31:20,280
- [Tom] Transportation servitive

835
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:21,867
provided by catty limousine.

836
00:31:21,867 --> 00:31:24,652
We get you there safe, or we don't pay.

837
00:31:24,652 --> 00:31:26,078
In Hannah's Port and Palm Beach.

838
00:31:26,078 --> 00:31:27,939
- [Joel] It's a speed bump with no tongue!

839
00:31:27,939 --> 00:31:30,522
(car skidding)

840
00:31:31,528 --> 00:31:33,434
- [Crow] He's an excellent driver.

841
00:31:33,434 --> 00:31:35,044
Definitely an excellent driver.

842
00:31:35,044 --> 00:31:37,321
He's not wearing his underwear.

843
00:31:37,321 --> 00:31:39,064
- [Joel] Man, I've been
following you around for days

844
00:31:39,064 --> 00:31:42,147
just hoping you might need a tow job.

845
00:31:44,564 --> 00:31:45,638
- You all right?

846
00:31:45,638 --> 00:31:46,761
- All right?

847
00:31:46,761 --> 00:31:48,814
- [Tom] All right, I'm
great, here, wait a minute.

848
00:31:48,814 --> 00:31:50,397
I'll let you look at me full-size.

849
00:31:50,397 --> 00:31:52,119
- I'm superb.

850
00:31:52,119 --> 00:31:53,087
(Tom hiccuping)

851
00:31:53,087 --> 00:31:55,504
No corners, I'm a round here.

852
00:31:57,591 --> 00:31:59,770
- [Crow] Is there an
interpreter in there with you?

853
00:31:59,770 --> 00:32:00,824
- Smith.

854
00:32:00,824 --> 00:32:04,366
Horatio Alger Smith.
- [Crow] Potato head.

855
00:32:04,366 --> 00:32:06,639
- [Joel] But you can call me sugar lumps.

856
00:32:06,639 --> 00:32:07,472
- How'd you get in the ditch?

857
00:32:07,472 --> 00:32:08,305
You fall asleep?

858
00:32:08,305 --> 00:32:09,138
- Oh, no, no.

859
00:32:09,138 --> 00:32:12,714
There was this big pink and black thing,

860
00:32:12,714 --> 00:32:14,393
drove right in front of me.
- [Crow] Uh huh.

861
00:32:14,393 --> 00:32:15,808
- It had stripes this wide.
- [Crow] Yeah,

862
00:32:15,808 --> 00:32:17,975
alcoholism sure is a hoot.

863
00:32:19,130 --> 00:32:20,113
- I'll get your car out.

864
00:32:20,113 --> 00:32:21,771
- Okay, that sounds like.

865
00:32:21,771 --> 00:32:22,991
- [Tom] Lean on me, baby.

866
00:32:22,991 --> 00:32:23,908
Yup, scene.

867
00:32:25,083 --> 00:32:27,240
Get moody up here, yup.

868
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,573
What's he doin'?

869
00:32:32,179 --> 00:32:33,262
- [Crow] Hey.

870
00:32:35,267 --> 00:32:37,784
- Hey, man, you can't drive this car.

871
00:32:37,784 --> 00:32:39,943
Fender's cutting the wheel.

872
00:32:39,943 --> 00:32:42,354
- Sure I can, the motor works, see.

873
00:32:42,354 --> 00:32:44,265
But that's for everything, dad.

874
00:32:44,265 --> 00:32:45,881
You're a cotton-pickin' prince.

875
00:32:45,881 --> 00:32:47,156
(laughing)

876
00:32:47,156 --> 00:32:49,122
(car revving)

877
00:32:49,122 --> 00:32:50,677
- Okay, just a second.

878
00:32:50,677 --> 00:32:51,972
I'll get out of the way.

879
00:32:51,972 --> 00:32:53,474
- [Crow] We thought it would be funny

880
00:32:53,474 --> 00:32:55,701
to make a hopeless
drunk try to drive a car

881
00:32:55,701 --> 00:32:56,981
while it's hooked to a tow truck.

882
00:32:56,981 --> 00:32:57,910
Let's watch.

883
00:32:57,910 --> 00:33:00,801
(car honking)

884
00:33:00,801 --> 00:33:01,634
- What is it?

885
00:33:01,634 --> 00:33:03,187
- [Tom] It's a State Farm insurance scene.

886
00:33:03,187 --> 00:33:04,722
You like it?

887
00:33:04,722 --> 00:33:06,770
- [Joel] This scene is funny.

888
00:33:06,770 --> 00:33:09,380
(laughing)

889
00:33:09,380 --> 00:33:11,425
- [Crow] Wide track tires
stabilize your ride.

890
00:33:11,425 --> 00:33:13,298
(car honking)

891
00:33:13,298 --> 00:33:14,563
- What is it, now?

892
00:33:14,563 --> 00:33:15,849
- [Tom] Oh, it's the Aamco theme.

893
00:33:15,849 --> 00:33:16,823
That's even better.

894
00:33:16,823 --> 00:33:18,531
- Steering wheel won't work.

895
00:33:18,531 --> 00:33:20,582
(laughing)

896
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:22,296
- [Joel] This strikes me as humorous.

897
00:33:22,296 --> 00:33:24,585
How can he drive when he's
hooked up to a tow truck?

898
00:33:24,585 --> 00:33:27,047
The whole concept strikes me as absurd.

899
00:33:27,047 --> 00:33:29,297
(laughing)

900
00:33:31,589 --> 00:33:32,876
(Crow sputtering)

901
00:33:32,876 --> 00:33:34,768
- [Crow] I'm driving. (sputtering)

902
00:33:34,768 --> 00:33:35,979
- [Joel] Honk honk!

903
00:33:35,979 --> 00:33:37,899
State Farm insurance.

904
00:33:37,899 --> 00:33:39,268
(hammering)

905
00:33:39,268 --> 00:33:41,858
- ♫ Rock my baby, she rocks ♫

906
00:33:41,858 --> 00:33:43,441
- [Crow] Get these spiders off me.

907
00:33:43,441 --> 00:33:45,807
(Crow whimpering)

908
00:33:45,807 --> 00:33:47,611
- ♫ My baby's a rock and roll lady ♫

909
00:33:47,611 --> 00:33:48,958
- [Tom] Rhythm, huh?

910
00:33:48,958 --> 00:33:50,156
(laughing)

911
00:33:50,156 --> 00:33:51,989
- [Crow] Huh, hold up.

912
00:33:54,975 --> 00:33:55,941
- [Tom] Oh, gee buddy,

913
00:33:55,941 --> 00:33:57,899
I hate a cappella.

914
00:33:57,899 --> 00:34:01,004
- [Chase] ♫ Sing, sing, sing
for a little diamond ring ♫

915
00:34:01,004 --> 00:34:02,460
- [Tom] Oh, so that's who I am.

916
00:34:02,460 --> 00:34:04,049
- [Chase] ♫ Swing and
sing and bells are ringing

917
00:34:04,049 --> 00:34:07,147
♫ Happy playing is
pleasure ringing, baby ♫

918
00:34:07,147 --> 00:34:09,006
- [Tom] Do, do-do, do-do, do-do.

919
00:34:09,006 --> 00:34:10,204
- [Chase] ♫ My baby she
- [Tom] Shut up!

920
00:34:10,204 --> 00:34:14,834
Shut up, shut up! (whimpering)

921
00:34:14,834 --> 00:34:17,690
- [Chase] ♫ Sing, rings
whenever I bring her things ♫

922
00:34:17,690 --> 00:34:18,690
- [Tom] Say.

923
00:34:20,593 --> 00:34:23,387
- [Joel] I think I'll take
after him with that handle.

924
00:34:23,387 --> 00:34:25,753
- [Chase] ♫ Swing and sing
and bells are ringing ♫

925
00:34:25,753 --> 00:34:29,836
("Mystery Science Theater 3000")

926
00:34:30,795 --> 00:34:32,738
- [Crow] Shut up, shut up, shut up!

927
00:34:32,738 --> 00:34:35,314
- [Chase] ♫ and baby ♫

928
00:34:35,314 --> 00:34:36,401
Good afternoon, Mr. Smith.

929
00:34:36,401 --> 00:34:37,698
- [Joel] Did I do something last night

930
00:34:37,698 --> 00:34:38,714
I'm not going to be proud of?

931
00:34:38,714 --> 00:34:42,346
- Guys have had their heads
chopped off for less than that.

932
00:34:42,346 --> 00:34:43,179
- For what?

933
00:34:43,179 --> 00:34:44,347
- [Crow] For singing,
a-singing, a-singing.

934
00:34:44,347 --> 00:34:47,083
- So doggone good when I feel so bad.

935
00:34:47,083 --> 00:34:49,010
How did I get here, anyway?

936
00:34:49,010 --> 00:34:51,788
- I towed you in this morning, remember?

937
00:34:51,788 --> 00:34:53,148
- [Tom] I towed you, but I left the car.

938
00:34:53,148 --> 00:34:55,170
- I remember very, very little.

939
00:34:55,170 --> 00:34:57,153
- [Joel] But don't worry,
you were a perfect gentleman.

940
00:34:57,153 --> 00:34:59,952
- I didn't see any other cars.

941
00:34:59,952 --> 00:35:02,170
- How'd you ever get
me in that bed, anyway.

942
00:35:02,170 --> 00:35:03,003
- [Tom] It was your cologne.

943
00:35:03,003 --> 00:35:04,200
- I carried you in there and I sat on you

944
00:35:04,200 --> 00:35:05,367
until you fell asleep.

945
00:35:05,367 --> 00:35:06,200
- [Joel] Oh, wow.

946
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:08,318
- Quite a chore.

947
00:35:08,318 --> 00:35:10,235
- You wouldn't have gotten
very far in your condition.

948
00:35:10,235 --> 00:35:11,256
- [Crow] It was fun, I didn't mind.

949
00:35:11,256 --> 00:35:13,240
- I appreciate it.

950
00:35:13,240 --> 00:35:14,073
- Chase Winston.

951
00:35:14,073 --> 00:35:14,906
- Chase.

952
00:35:16,604 --> 00:35:18,261
Mind telling how much I owe you?

953
00:35:18,261 --> 00:35:20,293
- Well, I bent the fender
out from the wheel.

954
00:35:20,293 --> 00:35:22,165
Want me to fill it in
and touch it up for you?

955
00:35:22,165 --> 00:35:23,427
- [Joel] Uh, you've touched enough, Chase.

956
00:35:23,427 --> 00:35:28,271
- I'll get that done when
I get back to the city.

957
00:35:28,271 --> 00:35:29,774
- [Tom] Yogurt?
- Coffee.

958
00:35:29,774 --> 00:35:31,183
- Oh, great.

959
00:35:31,183 --> 00:35:32,387
(slurping)

960
00:35:32,387 --> 00:35:33,317
- How 'bout two bucks.

961
00:35:33,317 --> 00:35:34,927
- [Crow] Two bucks, that's outrageous!

962
00:35:34,927 --> 00:35:35,760
I'm not paying.

963
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:38,210
- This coffee's worth
two bucks all by itself.

964
00:35:38,210 --> 00:35:39,681
How 'bout the tow?

965
00:35:39,681 --> 00:35:40,990
- No, I was coming this way anyway.

966
00:35:40,990 --> 00:35:44,271
Missed out on a little studying time.

967
00:35:44,271 --> 00:35:45,720
Make it three bucks?

968
00:35:45,720 --> 00:35:47,190
- [Tom] Kid, you're dumber
than a bag of hammers.

969
00:35:47,190 --> 00:35:50,544
- Sort of, I take a correspondence
course in engineering.

970
00:35:50,544 --> 00:35:52,526
- [Crow] Line city vo-tech.

971
00:35:52,526 --> 00:35:54,241
- I really feel indebted to you,

972
00:35:54,241 --> 00:35:56,603
and I'd like to do
something to pay you back.

973
00:35:56,603 --> 00:35:58,626
Next time you're in the
town, that's my card,

974
00:35:58,626 --> 00:35:59,551
look me up, will you?

975
00:35:59,551 --> 00:36:00,415
- Will do.

976
00:36:00,415 --> 00:36:01,310
- Okay.

977
00:36:01,310 --> 00:36:02,945
Oh, and by the way.

978
00:36:02,945 --> 00:36:03,923
- [Joel] Here's a Denny's coupon,

979
00:36:03,923 --> 00:36:06,255
good any time after midnight, enjoy.

980
00:36:06,255 --> 00:36:09,096
- Buy yourself a sponge rubber hammer man.

981
00:36:09,096 --> 00:36:09,929
(laughing)

982
00:36:09,929 --> 00:36:11,863
I'll see you, Chase.

983
00:36:11,863 --> 00:36:12,938
- Thank you.

984
00:36:12,938 --> 00:36:13,771
- [Crow] No, thank you!

985
00:36:13,771 --> 00:36:14,604
- [Tom] Oh no, thank you.

986
00:36:14,604 --> 00:36:15,437
- [Crow] No, thank you.

987
00:36:15,437 --> 00:36:17,220
- [Tom] No, please, thank you.

988
00:36:17,220 --> 00:36:19,259
- Steamroller Smith.

989
00:36:19,259 --> 00:36:20,425
The disc jockey!

990
00:36:20,425 --> 00:36:21,512
- [Joel] Hey, I love your morning show,

991
00:36:21,512 --> 00:36:25,679
especially when you make goofy
phone calls to celebrities!

992
00:36:27,672 --> 00:36:29,389
- Two 20's!

993
00:36:29,389 --> 00:36:31,722
- [Tom] That makes $30, wow!

994
00:36:34,656 --> 00:36:36,585
(chuckling)

995
00:36:36,585 --> 00:36:38,680
- [Crow] Well, she
swings whenever she sings

996
00:36:38,680 --> 00:36:43,256
whenever she sings, la da
dee da dee da dum dum dum.

997
00:36:43,256 --> 00:36:44,089
- Sheriff.

998
00:36:44,089 --> 00:36:45,404
- [Joel] I think you're
seeing too much of me.

999
00:36:45,404 --> 00:36:47,210
- Heard anything from Pat and Liz?

1000
00:36:47,210 --> 00:36:48,877
- No, nothing.

1001
00:36:48,877 --> 00:36:51,067
- Chase, I'm in a jam.

1002
00:36:51,067 --> 00:36:52,719
I need your help.

1003
00:36:52,719 --> 00:36:54,109
Wheeler swings a big enough
stick in this country

1004
00:36:54,109 --> 00:36:56,014
to make it rough.

1005
00:36:56,014 --> 00:36:57,019
And he's doing it.

