00:45:35,052 --> 00:45:36,213
- Okay?

1256
00:45:36,213 --> 00:45:37,312
Go ahead!

1257
00:45:37,312 --> 00:45:38,555
- [Crow] Should I go backwards?

1258
00:45:38,555 --> 00:45:39,972
- [Tom] Go ahead!

1259
00:45:42,031 --> 00:45:44,681
- [Crow] Um, I thought
you said go backwards.

1260
00:45:44,681 --> 00:45:46,857
- [Tom] That's right, go ahead!

1261
00:45:46,857 --> 00:45:49,754
- [Crow] Um,
- [Tom] Yes?

1262
00:45:49,754 --> 00:45:51,103
- [Crow] But should I go left?

1263
00:45:51,103 --> 00:45:52,457
- [Tom] Right!

1264
00:45:52,457 --> 00:45:54,288
- [Crow] Tell me, should I go left?

1265
00:45:54,288 --> 00:45:56,200
- [Tom] Right!

1266
00:45:56,200 --> 00:45:57,370
- [Crow] That's what I'm asking.

1267
00:45:57,370 --> 00:45:58,471
- [Tom] Right!

1268
00:45:58,471 --> 00:45:59,422
- [Crow] So this?
- [Tom] No left!

1269
00:45:59,422 --> 00:46:00,459
Ladies and gentlemen, join us next week

1270
00:46:00,459 --> 00:46:03,112
for another edition of Abbott
and Costello Playhouse.

1271
00:46:03,112 --> 00:46:05,565
(chuckling)

1272
00:46:05,565 --> 00:46:08,603
- [Joel] Folks, I tried to get
them to rewrite this scene.

1273
00:46:08,603 --> 00:46:10,701
Next time, I'll assist on final cut.

1274
00:46:10,701 --> 00:46:13,368
Enjoy my special spring project.

1275
00:46:15,372 --> 00:46:16,960
- That a girl, that a girl.

1276
00:46:16,960 --> 00:46:17,992
Keep going.

1277
00:46:17,992 --> 00:46:19,356
- [Tom] Crawl it over on us, now.

1278
00:46:19,356 --> 00:46:20,189
- Go five!

1279
00:46:22,482 --> 00:46:24,165
- [Tom] I really get a sense
of where that monster is,

1280
00:46:24,165 --> 00:46:25,284
don't you?

1281
00:46:25,284 --> 00:46:27,034
- [Crow] Mmhmm, yeah.

1282
00:46:31,166 --> 00:46:32,565
- You did fine, honey.

1283
00:46:32,565 --> 00:46:33,733
- [Crow] I'll be using
this condescending tone

1284
00:46:33,733 --> 00:46:35,765
'til the mid '70's.

1285
00:46:35,765 --> 00:46:38,488
- Yeah, we'll meet you
back at the garage, okay?

1286
00:46:38,488 --> 00:46:40,488
- Okay, let's go, Jenny.

1287
00:46:41,596 --> 00:46:43,516
- [Crow] Can't that woman use a door?

1288
00:46:43,516 --> 00:46:48,332
- [Joel] I sing whenever,
oh no, I'm doing it, oh.

1289
00:46:48,332 --> 00:46:50,832
(car revving)

1290
00:46:52,235 --> 00:46:55,433
- [Tom] Look, a cheese shredder.

1291
00:46:55,433 --> 00:46:57,153
- [Joel] Well, I'm getting really hungry.

1292
00:46:57,153 --> 00:46:59,017
I've gotta stop letting
them get away, folks.

1293
00:46:59,017 --> 00:47:02,517
Until next time, good night and God bless.

1294
00:47:03,916 --> 00:47:08,083
(Tom, Joel, & Crow humming
"The Munsters Theme")

1295
00:47:15,514 --> 00:47:16,450
- [Crow] So, the entire town revolves

1296
00:47:16,450 --> 00:47:18,060
around the towing business.

1297
00:47:18,060 --> 00:47:19,727
- [Tom] Pretty much.

1298
00:47:21,339 --> 00:47:23,256
- [Woman] See ya later.

1299
00:47:25,292 --> 00:47:28,538
- [Tom] He sings whenever
he sings whenever he sings!

1300
00:47:28,538 --> 00:47:29,705
Ah, forget it.

1301
00:47:30,810 --> 00:47:32,437
- [Crow] Hi, you guys fixin' cars?

1302
00:47:32,437 --> 00:47:34,088
Can I hang around some?

1303
00:47:34,088 --> 00:47:35,833
- What did you find?

1304
00:47:35,833 --> 00:47:37,988
- By the reservoir and William's wash,

1305
00:47:37,988 --> 00:47:39,556
they weren't in it.

1306
00:47:39,556 --> 00:47:41,283
No sign of blood or anything.

1307
00:47:41,283 --> 00:47:43,610
I think they were thrown clear.

1308
00:47:43,610 --> 00:47:44,663
- Search the area?

1309
00:47:44,663 --> 00:47:45,762
- [Tom] Isn't that your job?

1310
00:47:45,762 --> 00:47:47,912
- Down the ravine for about a mile.

1311
00:47:47,912 --> 00:47:50,216
Well, we looked beyond the wreck
for a couple hundred yards.

1312
00:47:50,216 --> 00:47:51,685
Wouldn't you say, Gordy?

1313
00:47:51,685 --> 00:47:53,052
- At least that far.

1314
00:47:53,052 --> 00:47:54,120
- You see any footprints?

1315
00:47:54,120 --> 00:47:55,721
- No, none.

1316
00:47:55,721 --> 00:47:57,766
- [Joel] Looks like Tige
Andrews in the middle there.

1317
00:47:57,766 --> 00:47:59,032
- [Tom] No, it's Larry Miller.

1318
00:47:59,032 --> 00:47:59,952
- [Joel] Larry Miller, huh?

1319
00:47:59,952 --> 00:48:01,730
- Drives the same as that Sedan.

1320
00:48:01,730 --> 00:48:04,433
Like it's been hit with
a 10 ton rubber mouth.

1321
00:48:04,433 --> 00:48:05,739
- [Tom] Is that a fantasy
of yours, Sheriff?

1322
00:48:05,739 --> 00:48:07,925
- Rough trip down that
cliff, but could've done it.

1323
00:48:07,925 --> 00:48:09,121
- Yeah.

1324
00:48:09,121 --> 00:48:11,054
I'll have to go over
that area with a rake.

1325
00:48:11,054 --> 00:48:12,865
- [Crow] You are a rake. (laughing)

1326
00:48:12,865 --> 00:48:15,766
- You know, I've been thinking,

1327
00:48:15,766 --> 00:48:17,582
if Liz and Pat had eloped,

1328
00:48:17,582 --> 00:48:18,905
