1329
00:48:18,905 --> 00:48:21,742
'Cause old man Wheeler would
have it traced right off.

1330
00:48:21,742 --> 00:48:23,231
- Well, maybe he stored it, Chase,

1331
00:48:23,231 --> 00:48:24,384
and then it was stolen.

1332
00:48:24,384 --> 00:48:26,594
- [Tom] Larry Miller, ladies
and gentlemen, Larry Miller.

1333
00:48:26,594 --> 00:48:27,925
- Somebody parked it there.

1334
00:48:27,925 --> 00:48:31,094
Well, the brakes could have
made it, rolled off the edge.

1335
00:48:31,094 --> 00:48:32,650
- It would be a strange coincidence

1336
00:48:32,650 --> 00:48:35,307
if they came back to
this part of the county.

1337
00:48:35,307 --> 00:48:37,849
Possibility makes some sense.

1338
00:48:37,849 --> 00:48:40,103
I'll get my gear and
dust for fingerprints.

1339
00:48:40,103 --> 00:48:42,020
- [Crow] Oh, Rochester,
will you dust the truck?

1340
00:48:42,020 --> 00:48:43,658
- Gosh, I wish you boys
would have called me

1341
00:48:43,658 --> 00:48:45,266
