This week, Director Ray Kellogg.

1917
01:09:46,808 --> 01:09:48,078
Ray Kellogg, of course was a--

1918
01:09:48,078 --> 01:09:49,695
- Cut, cut, excuse me Tom.

1919
01:09:49,695 --> 01:09:52,318
We've only got the one
camera, Cambot, okay?

1920
01:09:52,318 --> 01:09:53,725
- Oh, of course, thank you.

1921
01:09:53,725 --> 01:09:55,011
(clearing throat)

1922
01:09:55,011 --> 01:09:57,972
Ray Kellogg, much like his
good friend Orson Wells,

1923
01:09:57,972 --> 01:10:00,883
Kellogg's career was
short-circuited by his enormous ego

1924
01:10:00,883 --> 01:10:02,949
and his difficulties
in holding to a budget.

1925
01:10:02,949 --> 01:10:04,557
For example, in today's film,

1926
01:10:04,557 --> 01:10:05,940
the Gila monster affect

1927
01:10:05,940 --> 01:10:08,084
achieved at the use of a
normal sized Gila monster

1928
01:10:08,084 --> 01:10:11,222
and detailed sets filled
with twigs and matchbox cars

1929
01:10:11,222 --> 01:10:12,789
and it was enormously expensive

1930
01:10:12,789 --> 01:10:14,912
and there was virtually no
money left for blocking.

1931
01:10:14,912 --> 01:10:15,790
But Kellogg--

1932
01:10:15,790 --> 01:10:18,292
- 'Scuse me, don't you
think you should say a word

1933
01:10:18,292 --> 01:10:20,564
to the audience about
what blocking is, maybe?

1934
01:10:20,564 --> 01:10:22,530
- Don't mind me, it's only my show.

1935
01:10:22,530 --> 01:10:23,859
- Good, I'm glad you said that.

1936
01:10:23,859 --> 01:10:25,077
People of Earth,

1937
01:10:25,077 --> 01:10:27,010
blocking is a technique used by directors

1938
01:10:27,010 --> 01:10:29,376
to tell his actors where to stand

1939
01:10:29,376 --> 01:10:31,213
or maybe what to do with their bodies.

1940
01:10:31,213 --> 01:10:33,652
- Yeah, like in today's film.

1941
01:10:33,652 --> 01:10:34,656
You'll excuse me, Tom.

1942
01:10:34,656 --> 01:10:35,489
- Sure, fine.

1943
01:10:35,489 --> 01:10:36,965
- Well, the director just had the actors

1944
01:10:36,965 --> 01:10:38,348
put their legs up on everything.

1945
01:10:38,348 --> 01:10:39,924
- I was getting to that!

1946
01:10:39,924 --> 01:10:41,742
You see, it's called the leg up position.

1947
01:10:41,742 --> 01:10:43,166
- Maybe the leg up position is cheap,

1948
01:10:43,166 --> 01:10:44,878
but for Pete's sake, they're unrelenting.

1949
01:10:44,878 --> 01:10:46,350
They put their legs up on pipes,

1950
01:10:46,350 --> 01:10:47,597
on benches.
- [Tom] Stop it!

1951
01:10:47,597 --> 01:10:48,516
Joel, tell him to stop.

1952
01:10:48,516 --> 01:10:51,885
(all talking at once)

1953
01:10:51,885 --> 01:10:53,332
- This is his thing, you know.

1954
01:10:53,332 --> 01:10:54,560
- Oh, sorry.

1955
01:10:54,560 --> 01:10:55,408
- Thank you, Joel.

1956
01:10:55,408 --> 01:10:56,894
Beat it, buddy.

1957
01:10:56,894 --> 01:10:57,794
Well, I thank you.

1958
01:10:57,794 --> 01:10:58,830
Without further adieu,

1959
01:10:58,830 --> 01:11:00,786
