- [Tom] Conrad Bain!

1999
01:12:45,968 --> 01:12:48,608
- Do you mind telling me
what this is all about?

2000
01:12:48,608 --> 01:12:49,969
- Have you been down to the train wreck?

2001
01:12:49,969 --> 01:12:52,884
- [Crow] I'm the sheriff, what
would I be down there for?

2002
01:12:52,884 --> 01:12:55,362
- I talked to the trooper
about my son's car.

2003
01:12:55,362 --> 01:12:57,009
- [Tom] What, he's selling
his kid's car already?

2004
01:12:57,009 --> 01:12:58,133
- Shouldn't have been
moved until a thorough

2005
01:12:58,133 --> 01:13:00,207
investigation has been made

2006
01:13:00,207 --> 01:13:01,334
and it had been photographed.

2007
01:13:01,334 --> 01:13:02,319
- [Joel] Wait a minute, Conrad,

2008
01:13:02,319 --> 01:13:05,152
you wearing pants under that coat?

2009
01:13:06,461 --> 01:13:07,794
- I thought not.

2010
01:13:09,078 --> 01:13:13,035
That was removed and clues
lost without authority.

2011
01:13:13,035 --> 01:13:15,546
You didn't put that in your
report, did you, Sheriff.

2012
01:13:15,546 --> 01:13:16,702
- [Joel] Duh, huh?

2013
01:13:16,702 --> 01:13:17,903
- Of course, you didn't.

2014
01:13:17,903 --> 01:13:18,736
And I'll tell you why.
- [Joel] 'Cause you're

2015
01:13:18,736 --> 01:13:19,976
Earl Warren.

2016
01:13:19,976 --> 01:13:23,646
- You were protectin' that Chase Winston.

2017
01:13:23,646 --> 01:13:25,390
Covering him regardless the speck

2018
01:13:25,390 --> 01:13:27,067
it might have on others.

2019
01:13:27,067 --> 01:13:29,986
- [Crow] Chase Winston's a real booster.

2020
01:13:29,986 --> 01:13:31,531
- He's your son's friend,

2021
01:13:31,531 --> 01:13:34,458
probably the best one he's ever had.

2022
01:13:34,458 --> 01:13:35,994
Of course it wasn't in the report.

2023
01:13:35,994 --> 01:13:37,165
What good would it do.

2024
01:13:37,165 --> 01:13:38,243
- [Tom] Nobody reads those things.

2025
01:13:38,243 --> 01:13:42,332
- Any kid can make a mistake, Mr. Wheeler.

2026
01:13:42,332 --> 01:13:45,884
- Sheriff, it's my son that's missing.

2027
01:13:45,884 --> 01:13:47,654
- [Tom] Oh, throw that one up at me.

2028
01:13:47,654 --> 01:13:49,656
Twist the knife, why don't ya, ouch.

2029
01:13:49,656 --> 01:13:51,764
- [Joel] Are you a real sheriff?

2030
01:13:51,764 --> 01:13:54,377
- Have you heard the reports
about a giant lizard?

2031
01:13:54,377 --> 01:13:56,108
- [Tom] Yup, outta my jurisdiction.

2032
01:13:56,108 --> 01:13:58,297
- You believe 'em?

2033
01:13:58,297 --> 01:13:59,882
- I don't know, Mr. Wheeler.

2034
01:13:59,882 --> 01:14:01,493
Doesn't seem possible.

2035
01:14:01,493 --> 01:14:02,326
- Well why not?

2036
01:14:02,326 --> 01:14:03,352
They've been giants before.

2037
01:14:03,352 --> 01:14:05,583
- [Joel] There might be giants.

2038
01:14:05,583 --> 01:14:06,652
- How could anything that big

2039
01:14:06,652 --> 01:14:08,665
go unnoticed in this area?

2040
01:14:08,665 --> 01:14:10,860
- Have you ever walked the
length of William's wash?

2041
01:14:10,860 --> 01:14:11,693
- No.

2042
01:14:11,693 --> 01:14:12,526
- [Crow] Not naked.

2043
01:14:12,526 --> 01:14:13,359
- Know anybody that has?

2044
01:14:13,359 --> 01:14:14,712
- No.

2045
01:14:14,712 --> 01:14:17,278
- That area is so chocked with underbrush,

2046
01:14:17,278 --> 01:14:19,372
it isn't even good hunting ground.

2047
01:14:19,372 --> 01:14:22,121
And I say it is possible
for a giant lizard

2048
01:14:22,121 --> 01:14:24,894
to have lived there for
years without being seen.

2049
01:14:24,894 --> 01:14:26,635
- [Tom] Well, you're high, Conrad.

2050
01:14:26,635 --> 01:14:27,468
- Now.

2051
01:14:28,954 --> 01:14:30,572
- [Crow] This guy, he's like a puppet

2052
01:14:30,572 --> 01:14:31,981
made by Sid and Marty Krofft.

2053
01:14:31,981 --> 01:14:33,314
He hardly moves.

2054
01:14:35,314 --> 01:14:36,314
- [Tom] Yup.

2055
01:14:38,964 --> 01:14:41,352
- I can't blame you for
what's happened in the past,

2056
01:14:41,352 --> 01:14:44,249
but Compton's death is on your hands.

2057
01:14:44,249 --> 01:14:45,496
- How did you come to that conclusion?

2058
01:14:45,496 --> 01:14:46,801
- I'll tell you how.

2059
01:14:46,801 --> 01:14:48,022
- [Tom] I thought and I thought.

2060
01:14:48,022 --> 01:14:51,175
- Two miles beyond Pat's car.

2061
01:14:51,175 --> 01:14:53,092
And if you had investigated
that area thoroughly

2062
01:14:53,092 --> 01:14:54,905
as you're paid to do,

2063
01:14:54,905 --> 01:14:56,389
Compton might not have died.

2064
01:14:56,389 --> 01:14:58,589
- [Joel] Oh, quit funnin' me.

2065
01:14:58,589 --> 01:14:59,678
- Now, come out here,

2066
01:14:59,678 --> 01:15:02,205
I want to show you something else.

2067
01:15:02,205 --> 01:15:03,890
- [Tom] Uh oh.

2068
01:15:03,890 --> 01:15:06,092
- [Crow] You call this fixed?

2069
01:15:06,092 --> 01:15:07,819
- Our subject may have hit this car

2070
01:15:07,819 --> 01:15:10,368
but it didn't take the tires off.

2071
01:15:10,368 --> 01:15:11,887
And where are those new white sidewalls

2072
01:15:11,887 --> 01:15:14,767
on Chase Winston's hot rod come from?

2073
01:15:14,767 --> 01:15:16,114
- The lizard runs a chop shop?

2074
01:15:16,114 --> 01:15:17,420
- There was a towing charge against--

2075
01:15:17,420 --> 01:15:19,899
- He presumed the bill wouldn't be paid,

2076
01:15:19,899 --> 01:15:22,655
so he borrowed the tires in the meantime.

2077
01:15:22,655 --> 01:15:23,488
- Perhaps.

2078
01:15:23,488 --> 01:15:24,850
- That's thievery.

2079
01:15:24,850 --> 01:15:27,447
Destroying evidence and
obstructing justice.

2080
01:15:27,447 --> 01:15:30,011
Now, your last official act of office

2081
01:15:30,011 --> 01:15:32,950
will be to arrest that
boy and bring him in.

2082
01:15:32,950 --> 01:15:34,018
I'll go along

2083
01:15:34,018 --> 01:15:34,851
to ensure that it's done.
- [Tom] There's that

2084
01:15:34,851 --> 01:15:36,768
powerful gesture again.

2085
01:15:37,928 --> 01:15:39,436
- [Crow] Got me on that one.

2086
01:15:39,436 --> 01:15:41,807
(ominous music)

2087
01:15:41,807 --> 01:15:42,640
- [Tom] Sounds like a slow version of

2088
01:15:42,640 --> 01:15:44,190
"These Boots Are Made for Walking."

2089
01:15:44,190 --> 01:15:47,508
- [Joel] Are you ready to walk, boots?

2090
01:15:47,508 --> 01:15:50,835
I hate my life, it's (grunting).

2091
01:15:50,835 --> 01:15:53,485
(car revving)

2092
01:15:53,485 --> 01:15:55,024
- [Crow] Charo is playing.

2093
01:15:55,024 --> 01:15:57,132
- [Tom] Charo in charge? (laughing)

2094
01:15:57,132 --> 01:15:58,299
- [Crow] Yeah.

2095
01:15:59,949 --> 01:16:02,616
- [Tom] Barnaby Jones, epilogue.

2096
01:16:05,421 --> 01:16:06,828
- [Crow] It's a teen grope-fest.

2097
01:16:06,828 --> 01:16:08,719
(cheering)

2098
01:16:08,719 --> 01:16:12,189
(upbeat sockhop music)

2099
01:16:12,189 --> 01:16:15,189
- [Crow] Hey, the wallflower's here.

2100
01:16:16,507 --> 01:16:18,078
- [Tom] Now who invited Kim Curtis?

2101
01:16:18,078 --> 01:16:21,266
- [Crow] Must be related
to the producer Tim Curtis.

2102
01:16:21,266 --> 01:16:23,842
- Hey kids, a fella dropped
in over at KILT the other day.

2103
01:16:23,842 --> 01:16:25,293
- [Joel] He offered me
coke to play his record.

2104
01:16:25,293 --> 01:16:26,601
- A great new song.

2105
01:16:26,601 --> 01:16:27,617
I thought it was just fine.

2106
01:16:27,617 --> 01:16:28,591
I wanna play it for you.

2107
01:16:28,591 --> 01:16:30,301
We got a little pick-up group together,

2108
01:16:30,301 --> 01:16:32,784
and cut a demo disc on it.

2109
01:16:32,784 --> 01:16:33,709
I wanna play it for you,

2110
01:16:33,709 --> 01:16:34,831
and I'll see what you think about it.

2111
01:16:34,831 --> 01:16:36,078
- [Tom] It'll really
make you want a diary.

2112
01:16:36,078 --> 01:16:37,677
- The first person who
identifies the singer

2113
01:16:37,677 --> 01:16:39,986
on the record gets two free rides

2114
01:16:39,986 --> 01:16:42,110
on my elephant in Bangkok, Siam.

2115
01:16:42,110 --> 01:16:45,043
(laughing)

2116
01:16:45,043 --> 01:16:46,865
But you got to pay your
own over there and back.

2117
01:16:46,865 --> 01:16:49,355
- [Joel] Ooh, there's a stinger, ah.

2118
01:16:49,355 --> 01:16:50,666
- [Tom] Ouch (laughing).

2119
01:16:50,666 --> 01:16:53,503
(upbeat music)

2120
01:16:53,503 --> 01:16:54,610
- [Joel] It's Dionne Warwick.

2121
01:16:54,610 --> 01:16:55,476
- [Tom] The Dead Kennedys?

2122
01:16:55,476 --> 01:16:57,692
- [Crow] No, it's the
1910 Fruitgum Company.

2123
01:16:57,692 --> 01:16:58,797
- [Tom] Led Zeppelin?

2124
01:16:58,797 --> 01:17:02,397
- [Joel] No, no, nothing like that.

2125
01:17:02,397 --> 01:17:04,564
(yipping)

2126
01:17:07,138 --> 01:17:10,053
- [Crow] Whoa! Tige
Andrews, dancing up a storm

2127
01:17:10,053 --> 01:17:11,210
- [Joel] No, that’s Larry Miller.

2128
01:17:11,210 --> 01:17:12,877
- [Tom] Larry Miler.

2129
01:17:15,098 --> 01:17:18,262
- [Crow] Hey, there’s Jessica
Tandy in the back there.

2130
01:17:18,262 --> 01:17:19,929
- [Tom] She's dandy.

2131
01:17:24,436 --> 01:17:27,353
- [Joel] Hey, don't rush the stage.

2132
01:17:28,210 --> 01:17:29,128
- Hold your tar and feathers, yet.

2133
01:17:29,128 --> 01:17:30,145
I'm gonna play the rest of it.

2134
01:17:30,145 --> 01:17:31,097
How do you like?

2135
01:17:31,097 --> 01:17:32,098
(cheering)
- [Joel] It's got a good beat

2136
01:17:32,098 --> 01:17:33,827
and it's easy to dance to.

2137
01:17:33,827 --> 01:17:34,660
- Who's the singer?

2138
01:17:34,660 --> 01:17:35,493
- Elvis.

2139
01:17:35,493 --> 01:17:36,326
- [Crow] David Soul!

2140
01:17:36,326 --> 01:17:37,159
- [Tom] John Travolta!

2141
01:17:37,159 --> 01:17:37,992
- [Crow] Johnny Rivers!

2142
01:17:37,992 --> 01:17:38,825
- [Tom] Art Garfunkel!

2143
01:17:38,825 --> 01:17:39,787
- [Crow] Terence Trent D’Arby!

2144
01:17:39,787 --> 01:17:40,620
- [Tom] Johnny Thunders!

2145
01:17:40,620 --> 01:17:41,744
- But you lose.

2146
01:17:41,744 --> 01:17:44,788
Look, the same guy you
here singing on the record

2147
01:17:44,788 --> 01:17:45,621
also wrote the song.

2148
01:17:45,621 --> 01:17:47,025
Now, who is it?

2149
01:17:47,025 --> 01:17:48,615
(groaning)

2150
01:17:48,615 --> 01:17:50,698
- [Joel] Bobby Goldsboro?

2151
01:17:51,987 --> 01:17:53,886
- It's gonna come out on
records in a couple of months

2152
01:17:53,886 --> 01:17:55,458
and you can find his name on the label.

2153
01:17:55,458 --> 01:17:56,610
(crowd yelling)

2154
01:17:56,610 --> 01:17:57,619
- [Crow] Aw, we can't read!

2155
01:17:57,619 --> 01:17:58,664
- [Tom] Come on!

2156
01:17:58,664 --> 01:17:59,585
- I know it is.

2157
01:17:59,585 --> 01:18:01,118
- [Crowd] Who?

2158
01:18:01,118 --> 01:18:04,265
- [Joel] (foreign language)
Gary Lewis and the Playboys?

2159
01:18:04,265 --> 01:18:05,628
- Chase did it.

2160
01:18:05,628 --> 01:18:07,723
[Joel, Tom, & Crow] Kill him!

2161
01:18:07,723 --> 01:18:09,226
- Why didn't you say somethin'?

2162
01:18:09,226 --> 01:18:10,390
- [Voiceover] You didn't tell us.

2163
01:18:10,390 --> 01:18:11,518
- Well, I didn't know there was anything

2164
01:18:11,518 --> 01:18:12,759
I'd want to admit to.

2165
01:18:12,759 --> 01:18:13,592
(crowd talking)

2166
01:18:13,592 --> 01:18:16,024
- [Joel] Yeah, well
don't quit your tow job.

2167
01:18:16,024 --> 01:18:17,515
(crowd cheering and applauding)

2168
01:18:17,515 --> 01:18:18,552
- [Tom] Aw, this is sweet.

2169
01:18:18,552 --> 01:18:19,660
Just like when Vicki
Lawrence won the Grammy

2170
01:18:19,660 --> 01:18:21,827
on The Carol Burnett Show.

2171
01:18:23,471 --> 01:18:25,597
- [Crow] Thank you, thank you very much.

2172
01:18:25,597 --> 01:18:27,615
- Chase played me another little song.

2173
01:18:27,615 --> 01:18:29,074
It's kind of different from this one.

2174
01:18:29,074 --> 01:18:30,003
- [Joel] Different?

2175
01:18:30,003 --> 01:18:31,294
- But I imagine, with a little coaxing

2176
01:18:31,294 --> 01:18:33,075
by hitting your hands together like this,

2177
01:18:33,075 --> 01:18:34,453
he might give you a little preview of it.

2178
01:18:34,453 --> 01:18:35,286
What do you say?

2179
01:18:35,286 --> 01:18:36,919
(crowd applauding)
- [Joel] You mean like this!

2180
01:18:36,919 --> 01:18:38,336
- [Tom] Clapping!

2181
01:18:40,867 --> 01:18:42,801
- [Crow] You should have
washed it in cold water.

2182
01:18:42,801 --> 01:18:44,244
- [Joel] It’s a personal pan banjo.

2183
01:18:44,244 --> 01:18:45,328
(ukulele strumming)

2184
01:18:45,328 --> 01:18:48,461
- ♫ And the Lord said ♫

2185
01:18:48,461 --> 01:18:50,566
- [Tom] ♫ Tip toe through the tulips ♫

2186
01:18:50,566 --> 01:18:52,480
- [Chase] ♫ And the Lord said laugh ♫

2187
01:18:52,480 --> 01:18:54,099
- [Crow] Hey, see if you
can get your gun back

2188
01:18:54,099 --> 01:18:54,949
from the bouncer.

2189
01:18:54,949 --> 01:18:57,007
- ♫ Children laugh

2190
01:18:57,007 --> 01:18:58,621
♫ The Lord said laugh

2191
01:18:58,621 --> 01:19:00,210
♫ Children laugh ♫
(Tom whimpering)

2192
01:19:00,210 --> 01:19:02,859
- [Joel] And the Lord said
taste my lizard steel.

2193
01:19:02,859 --> 01:19:05,657
(Joel babbling as lizard)

2194
01:19:05,657 --> 01:19:07,382
- [Crow] Tonight, on Night Gallery

2195
01:19:07,382 --> 01:19:09,408
Lillian Hellman, Edward R. Murrow, and I

2196
01:19:09,408 --> 01:19:12,960
will sneak a smoke behind the bar.

2197
01:19:12,960 --> 01:19:17,343
- [Tom] I’d say music hath
charms to annoy a savage beast.

2198
01:19:17,343 --> 01:19:20,885
- [Joel] So, Sheriff's ready to do-si-do?

2199
01:19:20,885 --> 01:19:22,163
- [Tom] Matchbox.

2200
01:19:22,163 --> 01:19:22,996
Save ‘em. Buy ‘em all.

2201
01:19:22,996 --> 01:19:23,829
Collect them all.
- [Joel] No, those are

2202
01:19:23,829 --> 01:19:24,662
Hot Wheels.

2203
01:19:24,662 --> 01:19:25,495
- [Tom] Corgis, maybe.

2204
01:19:25,495 --> 01:19:26,995
- [Joel] Sizzlers.

2205
01:19:30,086 --> 01:19:33,069
(Tom, Joel, Crow snoring)

2206
01:19:33,069 --> 01:19:34,389
- [Chase] ♫ Children laugh ♫

2207
01:19:34,389 --> 01:19:35,962
- [Crow] Boy, you brought
the party to a complete halt.

2208
01:19:35,962 --> 01:19:37,250
- [Chase] ♫ The Lord said laugh

2209
01:19:37,250 --> 01:19:38,323
♫ Children laugh ♫

2210
01:19:38,323 --> 01:19:40,228
- [Tom] I'm guessing this is
the extended, boredom mix.

2211
01:19:40,228 --> 01:19:41,489
- [Chase] ♫ Children laugh

2212
01:19:41,489 --> 01:19:42,904
♫ The Lord said laugh

2213
01:19:42,904 --> 01:19:46,979
♫ Laugh, laugh ♫
- [Crow] Okay, just blend in.

2214
01:19:46,979 --> 01:19:47,812
- [Joel] We're from the committee

2215
01:19:47,812 --> 01:19:49,333
to keep rock n' roll white.

2216
01:19:49,333 --> 01:19:51,392
- [Chase] ♫ The Lord said laugh ♫

2217
01:19:51,392 --> 01:19:52,225
- Just a minute.

2218
01:19:52,225 --> 01:19:53,088
- [Crow] It gets better.

2219
01:19:53,088 --> 01:19:54,519
- ♫ The Lord said laugh

2220
01:19:54,519 --> 01:19:55,811
♫ Children laugh ♫

2221
01:19:55,811 --> 01:19:57,095
- [Joel] I just wanna
know if the Lord said it

2222
01:19:57,095 --> 01:19:59,161
this many times in a row.

2223
01:19:59,161 --> 01:20:01,794
- [Crow] That’s why
Deuteronomy is so long.

2224
01:20:01,794 --> 01:20:04,455
- ♫ That I created for you

2225
01:20:04,455 --> 01:20:07,756
♫ Riddled with joy from out of the blue ♫

2226
01:20:07,756 --> 01:20:08,648
(exploding)

2227
01:20:08,648 --> 01:20:11,067
(woman screaming)
- [Crow] It's Jeff Ruby!

2228
01:20:11,067 --> 01:20:12,605
(Joel babbling as lizard)

2229
01:20:12,605 --> 01:20:13,438
(eerie music)

2230
01:20:13,438 --> 01:20:14,938
- No, don't panic.

2231
01:20:16,462 --> 01:20:18,712
(grunting)

2232
01:20:19,974 --> 01:20:21,792
- [Joel] And the Lord
said die, children, die.

2233
01:20:21,792 --> 01:20:24,079
(Joel babbling as lizard)

2234
01:20:24,079 --> 01:20:25,595
- [Crow] Hey, you forgot to stamp my hand.

2235
01:20:25,595 --> 01:20:28,095
(eerie music)

2236
01:20:31,454 --> 01:20:35,869
- [Joel] Ow, quit
pushing back there, ouch!

2237
01:20:35,869 --> 01:20:39,952
("Mystery Science Theater 3000")

2238
01:20:41,210 --> 01:20:43,710
(eerie music)

2239
01:20:46,562 --> 01:20:47,802
(gun shooting)

2240
01:20:47,802 --> 01:20:51,969
- [Tom] Aw, he couldn't hit
the broadside of a barn dance.

2241
01:20:53,092 --> 01:20:53,925
(gun shooting)

2242
01:20:53,925 --> 01:20:55,592
- [Joel] Ow. Ow. Ow.

2243
01:20:59,485 --> 01:21:02,652
Hey, leave me along, I paid the cover.

2244
01:21:04,678 --> 01:21:05,598
I can take a hint.

2245
01:21:05,598 --> 01:21:09,217
I don't need a bomb to fall on me.

2246
